  "origin": "Todd Murphy (8 Coil Shakti software); signal templates licensed from Persinger & Koren",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "Todd Murphy's 'Limbic Workout' (descending lability batch) for the 8 Coil Shakti: seven 5-min signals for limbic structures, from the least to the most sensitive (chirp, caudate, Fibonacci, slow and standard hippocampus, short-latency and standard amygdala), with 90-s silences, over both temporal lobes. Murphy states that the brain gets 'a novel stimulation every few minutes' and so avoids habituation.",
  "notes": "Coils over both temporal lobes (Murphy's second choice), on the standard 8 Coil Shakti cross centred near T7/T8 (an inference from the vendor's chart); all eight run together, with no rotation or channel alternation (the vendor specifies none). Coil polarity follows the vendor's coil chart, one + and one - coil per stereo pair: C5 (top) and FT7 (front) on the left and T10 (bottom) and TP8 (back) on the right are reversed (weight -1), while T9, TP7, C6 and FT8 run as is. The vendor's session has 13 phases (7 signals of 5 min, each followed by 90 s of silence except the last; 44 min). This helmet allows 12 phases, so the silence between the slow and the standard hippocampal signal is left out (the slow signal is meant to 'prepare the hippocampus' for the standard one) and the session runs 42.5 min. The structure is verbatim on the vendor's page: 'This session is approximately 45 minutes. It uses seven signals. There is a 90 second silent gap between each phase, for a total of 13 phases', 'applying the various signals for five minutes each', in the order used here; the public demo does not include the session, and the vendor gives no alternation mode for it. Every waveform is proprietary. Chirp (Murphy: the modulated 40 Hz signal with gaps that get longer, amplitude and gaps varied by a Fibonacci constant): a sweep slowing from 40 to 6 Hz (the end frequency is a choice), 837 points at 3 ms once every 4 s, after the published FM pattern (837 points at 1 ms every 4 s); the 40 Hz phase modulation and the Fibonacci amplitude changes are not reproduced. Caudate: its waveform is unpublished, so the built-in accelerating burst stands in, as in the project's other caudate sessions, but with the default 1.5-s sweep (6 to 30 Hz, then 4 s of silence) instead of their 0.69 s, so that this phase differs from the two amygdala phases. Fibonacci: the project's Fibonacci-amplitude theta-burst construct (100 Hz pulse bursts at 5 Hz whose strength rises and falls along 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 ...). Standard hippocampus: 5 theta bursts of 4 pulses at 5.4 Hz (the vendor's LTP spectral peak) on Shakti's 3-ms points, then 4 s of silence. Slow hippocampus: the same template at 4-ms points, so the bursts and the time between them are a third longer (the vendor says both differ but gives no values; elsewhere its slow hippocampal files carry the codes tp_24_16 (kor_9_tp_24_16, 'Slow Hippocampal Signal - Fast Alternation') and ltp_24_16 (in the amygdala-left, slow-hippocampus-right file), whose numbers it does not explain, and whether this session uses either file is not stated). Amygdala: the built-in accelerating burst (6 to 30 Hz) of 230 points at 3 ms (0.69 s) with the standard 4-s silence; for the 'shorter latency' phase the silence is 2.3 s, so a burst starts every 3 s as in the published 230-point burst-firing pattern (the vendor gives no value). Vendor: 'USE THIS SESSION ONLY OVER BOTH SIDES OF YOUR HEAD.' The frontal-lobe version is murphy-shakti8-limbic-workout-frontal. The vendor reports headache or pressure in about 2% of users with the hippocampal signal (a figure it attributes to an earlier version of the technology); if so, lower the intensity by one third. The effects are vendor claims backed only by user reports. Independent double-blind tests found no field effect (Granqvist 2005; Gendle & McGrath 2012, the latter with the 8 Coil Shakti amygdala signal). Not for anyone with epilepsy or a seizure history, a psychiatric condition or medication, migraine or brain injury, or on drugs; this is not a treatment. Stop at once on fear or distress. Changed in this revision: the vendor's wording of the 13-phase structure, the slow-signal file code and the output page were added to the notes and sources; the phases are unchanged.",
  "setting": "The vendor's session takes about 45 min (42.5 min here). Darkness and silence for effects during the session; eyes closed, relaxed without meditating or falling asleep. Bilateral placement only.",
  "schedule": "Vendor's general Shakti rules: at most every 72 h or once a week, never on consecutive days; a series of 3 or 6 sessions, then a 21-day break.",
